------------------------------------------------------------
PATH MAPPING (documented — no silent drift)
------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated native-output path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/`
maps, in this repo's ADR-002 shared-source-group layout (project.yml: one `Sources/`
group feeds both the iOS `TeslaSync` and macOS `TeslaSync-macOS` app targets), to:

  apps/apple/Sources/DashboardWidgets/      <- surface (5 cohesive BatteryCellsWidget* files)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/DashboardWidgets/   <- XCTest bundle (TeslaSync-macOSTests / TeslaSyncTests)

This is the only location compiled into BOTH app targets without bespoke project surgery.
Files were split (5) to honor the swiftlint file_length<=400 rule; all share the
`BatteryCellsWidget` prefix:
  BatteryCellsWidget.swift           238 lines  (the View + previews)
  BatteryCellsWidgetComponents.swift 217 lines  (heatmap tiles, stat tiles, freshness chip, skeleton)
  BatteryCellsWidgetData.swift       229 lines  (BatteryCellSummary/BatteryCell decode + projection + a11y)
  BatteryCellsWidgetModel.swift      119 lines  (presentation resolver + @Observable view-model)
  BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift   115 lines  (dashboard-tier primitives + diagnostics sink)

Pre-existing project bug fixed (blocks the macOS gate, unrelated to this surface):
  project.yml TeslaSync-macOSTests TEST_HOST pointed at `TeslaSync-macOS.app`, but the
  macOS app target overrides PRODUCT_NAME=TeslaSync -> the app is `TeslaSync.app`. Added an
  explicit TEST_HOST to the macOS unit-test target so hosted tests can find their host.

------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web source reproduced)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources: useBatteryCells + useVehicles bound via the P1/S8 shared state-holder
  layer (KMP EnergyStore.batteryCells -> StateFlow<Resource<JsonElement>> -> StateHolderModel
  -> LoadableState), mirroring VehicleSettingsModel. No HTTP in the view.
- Composition: voltage heatmap grid (status tiles) + Min/Max/Avg/Spread stat tiles +
  (wide layout) Min/Avg/Max temperature row. Responsive: cols<=1 compact (2-col),
  cols>=3 wide (4-col, +temps), else 3-col. Cell deviation status thresholds 5/15 mV
  reproduced (BatteryCellStatus.classify); fmtNumber/safeNumber parity (BatteryCellsProjection.fixed).
- States (all rendered): loading (skeleton), empty ("No battery cell data"),
  inner empty ("No cell data"), loaded, stale (chip), offline (cached + offline chip),
  error (QueryError + retry).
- i18n: all 11 source keys via translation.widget.batteryCells.* (P1/S10 catalog), plus
  widget.freshness.{live,stale,offline,accessibility} + translation.common.{retry,refresh,loading}.
  No English string literals in native code.
- Accessibility: combined VoiceOver labels on tiles/chips, freshness a11y label,
  Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS), reduce-motion honored (TSSkeleton shimmer gated).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): emits view.opened with surface slug "BatteryCellsWidget" on appear
  (DashboardWidgetTelemetrySink; maps onto ADR-016 ScreenView at the diagnostics boundary).

